\section{Transformers}

\subsection{Structure and Faraday's law}
A transformer has a primary coil, a secondary coil, and usually a laminated
\textbf{soft-iron core} linking them.

Alternating primary current $\Rightarrow$ alternating magnetic flux in the core
$\Rightarrow$ changing flux through the secondary $\Rightarrow$ induced secondary
emf (Faraday). Steady d.c.\ in the primary gives steady flux after switch-on,
so $\Delta\Phi/\Delta t=0$ and no sustained secondary emf.

